IMPORT prelude

§ `Codex Insurance Limited: Policy Rules`

-- This module encodes the substantive rules of the policy: when a
-- hospitalization claim is covered, and what defeats coverage. It defines
-- rules only -- no specific claim's facts are given a value here. Per-claim
-- data belongs in the file that imports this one.
--
-- Per the task's instructions, the agreement is assumed signed and the
-- premium assumed paid on time (Section 1.1, items 1 and 2), so those two
-- sub-conditions of "the policy will be in effect" are not modelled below.
--
-- All times below, other than the claimant's age, are modelled as NUMBERs
-- of months elapsed since the policy's effective date (queries give times
-- this way directly), so no DATE arithmetic is needed anywhere in this file.

§§ `Vocabulary`

-- Section 2.1: the specific activities whose resulting sickness or injury
-- is excluded from cover. Other is every hospitalization cause not on that
-- list -- e.g. an illness, or an accident unconnected with any of them.
DECLARE `Cause of Hospitalization` IS ONE OF
    Skydiving
    `Military Service`
    `Firefighter Service`
    `Police Service`
    Other

-- The facts of a single hospitalization claim made against the policy.
-- A type only: this file defines no claim data, only the shape of it.
DECLARE Claim HAS
    -- Section 2.1: what the sickness or accidental injury arose out of.
    -- Merely being employed in one of the excluded services does not, by
    -- itself, make this the excluded cause -- only an injury that itself
    -- arose out of that service does.
    `cause of hospitalization`    IS A `Cause of Hospitalization`
    -- Section 2.1, item 5: the claimant's age, in years, at the time of
    -- the hospitalization. The one time-related fact NOT relative to the
    -- effective date.
    `age at hospitalization`      IS A NUMBER
    -- How many months after the policy's effective date the
    -- hospitalization occurred.
    `hospitalization month`       IS A NUMBER
    -- Section 1.3: how many months after the effective date the wellness
    -- visit itself took place -- or NOTHING if it has not taken place yet.
    `wellness visit month`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- Section 1.3: how many months after the effective date written
    -- confirmation of that visit was supplied to the Company -- or
    -- NOTHING if it has not been supplied yet.
    `wellness confirmation month` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    -- Section 1.2: whether the claimant committed fraud, misrepresentation,
    -- or material withholding of information in connection with the policy.
    `fraud or misrepresentation`  IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `2. General Exclusions`

GIVEN cause IS A `Cause of Hospitalization`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`arises from an excluded activity` cause MEANS
    CONSIDER cause
    WHEN Skydiving             THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Military Service`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Firefighter Service` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Police Service`      THEN TRUE
    WHEN Other                 THEN FALSE

-- Section 2.1, item 5.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded by age` claim IF
    claim's `age at hospitalization` AT LEAST 80

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `excluded event` claim IF
       `arises from an excluded activity` (claim's `cause of hospitalization`)
    OR `excluded by age` claim

§§ `1.3 The Wellness Visit Condition`

-- The visit itself must occur no later than the 6th month anniversary of
-- the effective date. If it has not happened yet, it only counts as late
-- once that 6-month deadline has already passed as of the hospitalization
-- (before then the condition is still pending, per Section 1.1, item 3).
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness visit occurred late` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness visit month`
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m GREATER THAN 6
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 6

-- Written confirmation of the visit must be supplied no later than the
-- 7th month anniversary of the effective date. Same "not yet due" logic
-- as above, one month later.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`wellness confirmation submitted late` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim's `wellness confirmation month`
    WHEN JUST m  THEN m GREATER THAN 7
    WHEN NOTHING THEN claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 7

-- Section 1.3 as a whole: either half being late defeats the condition.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `condition on the wellness visit violated` claim IF
       `wellness visit occurred late` claim
    OR `wellness confirmation submitted late` claim

§§ `1.2 Cancelation`

GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy canceled` claim IF
       claim's `fraud or misrepresentation`
    OR `condition on the wellness visit violated` claim
    OR claim's `hospitalization month` GREATER THAN 12

§§ `1.1 Policy in Effect`

-- Items 1 and 2 (signed; premium paid) are assumed true, per instructions,
-- and so do not appear here. Item 3 (the Section 1.3 condition is pending
-- or satisfied) is NOT (condition on the wellness visit violated); item 4
-- (not canceled) and item 3 are both folded into `policy canceled` above.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `policy in effect` claim IF
    NOT (`policy canceled` claim)

§§ `Coverage Decision`

-- Section 3.1: the policy insures worldwide, 24 hours a day, so there is
-- no geographic condition or exclusion to encode. Sections 3.2-3.5
-- (arbitration, currency, governing law, premium timing) are procedural
-- and do not bear on whether a given hospitalization is covered, so they
-- are not modelled either. Section 3.6 (one-year term) is encoded above,
-- inside `policy canceled`.
GIVEN claim IS A Claim
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `covered` claim IF
        `policy in effect` claim
    AND NOT (`excluded event` claim)
